00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:25.040
Kamogawa Christmas

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.330
That was a double whammy, wasn't it, Madoka?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.500
Your report card and post-graduation plans.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.580
Yeah, I guess...

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.170
But I'll be busy during Christmas.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:34.960
Huh?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.300
Starting with this!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.840
A going-away party?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.930
Kirius and Array are going back to their home planet,

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.390
so we thought of doing a going-away/Christmas party for them.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.230
I want to give them a big send-off.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.020
What?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.730
Isn't the Jersey Club always busy around Christmas with requests for help?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.980
A going-away party on top of that?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.320
Can you manage?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.450
No problem!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.620
This year, it's not just me!

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.500
We still haven't tracked down Moid.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.370
We've made inquiries to Le Garite,

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.630
but they claim he hasn't been back.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.040
What about Dizelmine?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.550
Have you asked him directly?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.760
Yes.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.430
I asked him after explaining the situation,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.840
but I received the same reply.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.350
Moid is now a wanted man throughout the Polyhedron,

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.480
but we have no clues to his whereabouts after he left Pharos.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:31.640
I see...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.650
<i>It's been 20,000 years...</i>

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.070
<i>Now, let's go.</i>

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.370
Even after watching this so many times, it never ceases to amaze me.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.910
How that stone tablet could become so small.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.170
It's beyond current human logic.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.250
That's technology from the age when the Vox were created.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.300
Moid is able to use it

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.840
because he's a human from 20,000 years ago.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.600
<i>"The giant green demon will rip the heavens..."</i>

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.930
<i>"The giant blue demon will devour the stars..."</i>

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.520
<i>"The giant orange demon will spew out darkness..."</i>

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.610
<i>"Through countless sacrifices, they will rule the land..."</i>

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.780
It's an old tale told in Le Garite.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.660
As you all know, it tells of the tragedy brought on by the Vox.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.450
Just for the record,

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.160
the person who piloted that Vox... was me.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.540
What?!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.460
My real name is Maycun.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.460
I was the queen of a nation that existed here 20,000 years ago,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.670
known as Le Garite.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.390
Why have you kept this from us until now?

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.100
Because I thought you wouldn't believe me.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.350
I thought perhaps I could do something

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.520
to prevent the same tragedy from happening again...

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.230
That is why I returned.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:07.030
Moid, however, probably has other plans.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.580
We need to find him as soon as possible.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.580
You know, I wish you had told us sooner.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.330
Huh?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.340
You're the one who handpicked

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.050
each of us from around the globe, remember?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.010
Everyone...

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.390
I have a ton of questions I want to ask you.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:38.150
But first, people, contact Polyhedron again and find Moid!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.190
Yes, sir!

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:54.160
Kirius, why didn't you put a cover on your Ovid?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.620
Man, you can be so lazy!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.870
And because of that,

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.170
we're ending up having to do more work. You-

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.590
I wasn't being lazy.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.420
What was it, then?

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.800
It's unsightly.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.760
It's bad enough that we have them parked on a harbor,

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.600
so just deal with it.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.850
True.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.180
Hey!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.850
You guys hungry?

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.110
So you're going home, eh?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:24.900
Yes.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.190
Thank you for all your help.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.700
What're you going to do when you go back?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.990
I intend to take over as the head of my family.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.570
Huh?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.740
Kirius comes from a very proper noble family.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.950
But it seems they're going through some difficult times right now.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.000
Really?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.670
So you're a rich kid.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.290
How about you, Array?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.380
I'm thinking of becoming an instructor at the Royal Academy.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.010
A teacher, huh!

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.260
That might just suit you.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.140
You're not the nitpicky sort.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.640
I won't be dressed in these clothes, though.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.470
Oh yeah, so I hear you're not going back?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.430
Huh?

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.270
Uh...yeah...

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.060
I plan on training to become a cook.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.440
I see... You're staying on Earth.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.650
If I quit now, it'll feel like I gave up part way.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.910
If I continue a bit longer, I think I'll find something.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.580
Yeah.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.870
You've got backbone, all right.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.960
You can call me "Old Man," if you'd like.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:21.960
Why?

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.380
Okay!

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.880
Let's do this!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.390
We have a winner!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.010
Third prize is a Christmas cake.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.560
Congratulations.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.310
Who's next?

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.650
Oh, Ms. Machiko!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.440
I hope you win the grand prize - the big-screen TV!

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:49.190
Kyono, aren't you forgetting something?

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:49.740
Huh?

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.610
Your post-graduation plans.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:56.240
Oops! But I have a packed schedule today...

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.290
Bring it to me tomorrow!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:01.960
Wow!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.170
Ms. Machiko, you hit the jackpot!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.750
The Kamogawa Prize!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.960
A room for two and a lavish dinner!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:08.840
Wow!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.090
Congratulations!

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.760
Who will you be going with?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.680
With Youko! You got a problem with that?!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.470
Why is she angry when she won?

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.270
Madoka...

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.650
Hi, kids!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.440
Santa's here!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.110
We brought presents for all the good boys and girls!

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.030
Yay!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.570
Okay, one at a time!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.200
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:36.950
Stop that!

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.870
All right, line up in a straight line!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.500
Okay!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:44.620
Success!

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.920
How fun!

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:49.710
Sorry we're late.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.380
We've been waiting for you, Jersey Club!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.550
Oh, three this year?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.680
Yes! We have three times the youth!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.630
That was so much fun!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.380
What a wonderful Christmas!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.170
Yeah!

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.880
We have Lan's brother and Big Brother Giuvi to thank

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.430
for being able to do all these Jersey Club activities.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.560
If it weren't for them, the Polyhedron would still be fighting,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.310
and we wouldn't be enjoying Christmas like this.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.520
Everyone working together and being happy is the best!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.690
Agreed.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:53.900
Is this how you spend your Christmas every year, Madoka?

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:54.320
Yup!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.150
Always. And next year...

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.120
Are you okay?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.500
Snow!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.420
No wonder it's so cold.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.540
So pretty.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:20.340
The colors of spring, summer, autumn and winter.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.140
They're all so different.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.810
It's fun to see them change.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.850
It's just like Madoka.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:28.810
Huh?

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.500
My vote goes to Izo for who cries first.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.500
Then I vote for Kirius.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.340
I'll go with Array.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:03.350
Going-Away 
party

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:03.350
For Kirius 
and Array

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:03.350
For Kirius 
and Array

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.340
But won't Izo be the one seeing them off?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.390
Those three have been together all this time.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.680
For Kirius 
and Array

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.680
For Kirius 
and Array

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:07.640
It will be hard on Izo to be separated from those two.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.730
Array and Kirius will be separated too,

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.730
once they return to their home planet.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:13.020
In that case,

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.610
I'll vote for all three crying at the same time.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:20.150
The three of them found their paths in life.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.490
Yeah...

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.660
Their path in life?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.410
Oh...

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:27.830
Your post-graduation plans.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.870
When I think about it,

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:34.170
I feel like steam's going to come out of my head.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.920
My head's hot...

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:40.550
Huh?

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.260
Are you overheating?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:44.970
She's right. It's hot!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.720
I think you have a fever.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.310
Something to eat might make it go away...

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.600
Madoka!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.440
This is supposed to be good for you, so I made some.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.820
Pickled plums?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:03.360
Uh-huh.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.990
I wonder what it tastes like...

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.580
You've never had pickled plums before?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.580
Want to try?

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.170
Does it taste bad?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.050
No, it's delicious.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.840
Right?

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.380
You know...

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.600
Since coming here, I've been able to try lots of different foods.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.520
On Le Garite, I was a very picky eater.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.730
Kamogawa is a great place, isn't it?

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:38.360
Yes.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.820
Muginami...

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.370
Lan, Muginami!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.530
Over here...

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.830
It's becoming untied...

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.210
Lan, did you submit your post-graduation plan?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.790
I see...

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:00.750
Did you, Muginami?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:05.510
I want to do something to help my home planet U-Go.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.350
That's why I'm planning to return to De Metrio.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.810
Same here.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.560
I want to help my brother.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.060
How should we break the news to Madoka?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:19.270
Don't know...

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:24.650
Madoka probably thinks we're going to stay here forever.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:32.540
But it was Madoka who helped me make up my mind.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.750
I know. Madoka helped me change, as well.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.170
Thanks to her, I know I can help my brother now.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.130
She'll understand, won't she?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.380
She will.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.050
After all...

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.220
We're one now.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.450
How's the analysis of the stone tablet coming?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.040
You're pushing yourself too hard.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.500
Rest a bit.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.500
Thank you.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.880
But I can't take a break while making the crew work.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:30.640
It's not your fault that you lost your memory.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.140
It's time you let go of the past, that burden you've been carrying.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.680
If you don't, you won't get any work done.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.320
Everyone looked stunned...

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.440
Can you blame them?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.990
<i>Then, Ms. Chairman, how old does that really make you?</i>

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.700
<i>Let's just say 20,010 years old.</i>

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.790
And so,

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.290
here's to the future of these three young men.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.710
Cheers!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.840
Cheers!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.300
Array...

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.640
Kirikiri...

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.970
This song's for you!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.230
<i>This must be pretty serious to warrant a top-secret call.</i>

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.100
Yes.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.860
There's something we need to talk about.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.570
<i>Is this about Moid?</i>

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.570
Who is he?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:33.240
I rechecked his history in the Le Garite database,

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.080
but other than being a top Vox researcher,

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.370
there's nothing else there.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.870
When did he become Dizelmine's aide?

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.500
<i>He's been associated with the Le Garite royal family for quite some time now.</i>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.340
Have you met with Dizelmine lately?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:50.920
<i>Yes...</i>

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.340
You haven't, have you?

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:56.350
<i>He's using Moid and planning something.</i>

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.760
<i>Is that what you're thinking?</i>

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:58.970
Exactly.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.390
<i>I don't know what Moid is up to,</i>

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.560
<i>but I can't believe Dizelmine has anything to do with it.</i>

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>Besides, wasn't it Novumundus that assigned Moid to Pharos as a "bridge person"</i>

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.910
<i>between Polyhedron and Earth?</i>

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.410
A bridge?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.910
That's right! That has to be it!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.540
<i>What is it?</i>

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.120
It's nothing...

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.710
Anyhow, let me know if you uncover anything.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:24.710
<i>Sure...</i>

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.000
Bridge...

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.590
"The Bridge Person of Neuenkirchen."

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.590
If I apply that algorithm...

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.010
With all due respect...

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:42.180
Why do you continue to cover for the king of Le Garite even in this situation?

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.230
I'm not covering for him.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.270
Then why?

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.070
When we had our run-in the other day,

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.110
I remembered how we did the same thing in the past.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:56.910
20,000 years ago, our ancestors found a new world

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.700
where they gave birth to the Polyhedron nation.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.200
Dizelmine argued that in order to maintain this hard-earned peace,

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:07.130
the people must have a single, strong leader.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.960
And then he exiled you, Lord Villagiulio,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.090
to Planet U-Go for questioning his decision.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.470
He used you as an example to the others.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.510
That's not quite right.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.600
At the time,

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.770
he thought I had betrayed him and allied with the opposition.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.100
Betrayed him?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.310
No one would follow Dizelmine's despotic way of thinking in the first place!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.230
Forgive me.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.480
More than anyone,

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.150
he wishes for peace within the Polyhedron.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.280
It is also my wish as well.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.780
And that is why you tried to make peace with him

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.540
at the Intergalactic Conference.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.250
But look at the result.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:48.500
This time, I want to believe him until the very end.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:52.130
I want to believe in that strong passion of his.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.350
Your Majesty, shall we call it a day?

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:05.430
<i>If I may, sir...</i>

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.190
<i>Even though this is the only way to achieve</i>

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:11.730
<i>your greatest wish of protecting the peace of the Polyhedron.</i>

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:15.150
<i>I am still very honored that you have agreed to my suggestion.</i>

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.110
Enough talk.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:17.070
Continue.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.490
As you wish.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.460
You will...

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.880
never betray me...again...

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.550
Villagiulio!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.850
Lan, you did your best, good job!

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.390
<i>Now in closing,</i>

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:50.400
<i>let's have Array and Kirius say a few words!</i>

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.440
Uh... Thank you for putting together

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:57.490
such a wonderful party for us today.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.860
Almost makes me want to...

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.410
I really appreciate all of you.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:09.120
We will never forget the days we spent here in Kamogawa.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.330
I want to say thank you in so many ways,

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.210
but that would sound cliché, so...

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.090
Uh, I...

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.890
I will be remaining here for a while, but...

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:31.390
Now that these three will be setting out on their new journey,

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:35.480
it brought back memories of how we all first met.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:39.110
The whole idea of letting aliens work for me part-time sounded crazy!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.240
Or, so I thought.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.910
But you turned out to be really awesome guys!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.580
I'm gonna miss you!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.540
Damn, I think I'm gonna cry!

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:50.460
Boss!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:54.710
Uncle Hiroshi...

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.380
I didn't see that one coming.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.590
Yeah, they're crying their eyes out.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.300
Hey.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.590
Oh, Big Sis.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.010
You're late.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.550
Sorry.

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:06.510
Looks like it was a nice going-away party.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.060
Yeah.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:13.230
Here.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.100
When we told them you guys were leaving,

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.860
the people over at the shopping district gave us all these!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.110
Look at all this!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:21.780
Take care!

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.700
Suc...cess!

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:42.800
It's...

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.180
a Memoria!

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.390
A planet that shines brighter than De Metrio...

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.850
This once-dead planet has become brilliant again, hasn't it?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.540
Care to explain the meaning of this?

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.620
I'm sorry.

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.790
I haven't done it yet.

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.460
I understand it's hard to decide,

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.420
but in a few months, you'll be forced to face that reality.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:22.550
Why can't you write something?

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.170
